WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.990
Next question today is David.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:07.019
So in the end, should Michael Bloomberg be
allowed into the democratic presidential debates?

00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:13.900
So I've said this before, the DNC created
their rules for getting into the debates and

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.250
if they want to live by those those rules,
they have to die by those rules unless they

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.510
simply change them to let Michael Bloomberg
in and they've changed them.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:28.850
And uh, the, the big change is that the early,
um, the, the donor requirements have been

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.770
eliminated for upcoming debates and indeed
Michael Bloomberg may get into.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:37.400
And by the time you even watch this clip,
it's possible he may have already qualified

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.540
for one of the upcoming democratic debates.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.610
So it depends on how you ask this question.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:52.180
If you ask me, is this a calculated establishment
move to try to give another a more centrist

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.270
Democrat?

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.030
He's been a lifelong Republican, but okay.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.500
He's a Democrat now and he's a centrist Democrat
at that.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.620
The idea is put someone else in there who
might be able to deny a progressive, the presidency

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.280
who might be able to split the delegate counts
such that nobody wins.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:13.119
50% plus one delegates on the first round
of voting at the DNC, such that super delegates

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:16.490
then come in and they can pick whoever they
want.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.759
Then if that's the framing, then the answer
is no.

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:23.499
This is another way that the DNC is putting
their thumb on the scale against progressive

00:01:23.499 --> 00:01:26.350
candidates in a democratic primary.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:33.810
If you simply say to me, if someone's polling
third around 14 15% should they be in the

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:34.810
debates?

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:36.329
Dancers like, well, yeah, they should.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.329
Right?

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:42.439
I mean, if, when we talk about people seeing,
continuing to say, Andrew Yang never should

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:46.299
have canceled his campaign, we want his voice
at the debate.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:47.859
We want more voices at the debates.

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:53.039
We want tools, C's voice, despite the fact
that she has not a path to a single delegate.

00:01:53.039 --> 00:01:55.889
If you want more voices, even if you don't
like them, right?

00:01:55.889 --> 00:01:57.219
It can't be out of personal bias.

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:00.560
It has to really be, you want more voices?

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.969
How do you say the guy who's polling third
nationally right now shouldn't be in the debates?

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:15.120
So I simultaneously recognize that the entire
Bloomberg thing is people who are desperate

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:21.079
to prevent a progressive from being nominated
who are seeing Biden falter and Buddha edge

00:02:21.079 --> 00:02:27.010
edge maybe become the establishment choice,
but he still got issues and Amy Klobuchar

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:31.370
doesn't seem to, there is a desperation for
maybe Bloomberg could come in and pick this

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.190
entire thing up or at least deny a progressive
the nomination.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.190
That's terrible.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.500
I hate that.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.060
If you say someone's in third place, should
they be on the stage?

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.459
The answer is like, yeah, they should.

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:45.569
They should be on the stage and uh, if their
ideas are bad, they should be exposed as bad

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:46.750
on the stage.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:52.129
So it's, there is not a clear answer here
without being a supporter of Michael Bloomberg's,

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:57.690
I don't find there to be a strong ideological
case to say the guy in third place shouldn't

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.540
be in the debates change my mind.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.370
